    <custom_item>
      type                 : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description          : "1.66 O365-EX-000034"
      info                 : "File attachments from Outlook must be opened in Excel in Protected mode.

GROUP ID: V-223343
RULE ID: SV-223343r961092

This policy setting allows you to determine if Excel files in Outlook attachments open in Protected View.

If you enable this policy setting, Outlook attachments do not open in Protected View.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Outlook attachments open in Protected View."
      solution             : 'Set policy value for

User Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Microsoft Excel 2016 >> Excel Options >> Security >> Trust Center >> Protected View >> Turn off Protected View for attachments opened from Outlook

to \'Disabled\'.'
      reference            : "800-171|3.13.13,800-171r3|03.13.13,800-53|SC-18(4),800-53r5|SC-18(4),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001170,CSF|DE.CM-5,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-18(4),LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SU3,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-223343r961092_rule,STIG-ID|O365-EX-000034,Vuln-ID|V-223343"
      see_also             : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26066"
      value_type           : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data           : "0"
      reg_key              : "HKU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Office\16.0\Excel\Security\ProtectedView"
      reg_item             : "DisableAttachmentsInPV"
      reg_ignore_hku_users : "S-1-5-18,S-1-5-19,S-1-5-20,S-1-5-80"
      reg_option           : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.67 O365-LY-000001"
      info        : "The SIP security mode in Lync must be enabled.

GROUP ID: V-223344
RULE ID: SV-223344r1043178

When Lync connects to the server, it supports various authentication mechanisms. This policy allows the user to specify whether Digest and Basic authentication are supported. Disabled (default): NTLM/Kerberos/TLS-DSK/Digest/Basic Enabled: Authentication mechanisms: NTLM/Kerberos/TLS-DSK Gal Download: Requires HTTPS if user is not logged in as an internal user."
      solution    : 'Set the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Skype for Business 2016 >> Microsoft Lync Feature Policies \'Configure SIP security mode\'

to \'Enabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.13.15,800-171r3|03.13.15,800-53|SC-23,800-53r5|SC-23,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001184,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-23,ITSG-33|SC-23a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-223344r1043178_rule,STIG-ID|O365-LY-000001,Vuln-ID|V-223344"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26066"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Office\16.0\Lync"
      reg_item    : "EnableSIPHighSecurityMode"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.68 O365-LY-000002"
      info        : "The HTTP fallback for SIP connection in Lync must be disabled.

GROUP ID: V-223345
RULE ID: SV-223345r1043178

Prevents from HTTP being used for SIP connection in case TLS or TCP fail."
      solution    : 'Set the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Skype for Business 2016 >> Microsoft Lync Feature Policies \'Disable HTTP fallback for SIP connection\'

to \'Enabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.13.15,800-171r3|03.13.15,800-53|SC-23,800-53r5|SC-23,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001184,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-23,ITSG-33|SC-23a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-223345r1043178_rule,STIG-ID|O365-LY-000002,Vuln-ID|V-223345"
